-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",237,{
[7553]="70019504\n1\tUse Major Ballad while in combat with the Training Dummy\tHINT: Minstrels use Ballads to attack their enemies, lightly heal their fellows and empower themselves. These skills operate on a rotating system that allows the minstrel to have three special buffs on themselves at any time. After the third buff is applied the next Ballad played will overwrite the first, then the second and so on.\n2\tTalk to the Minstrel Trainer in Archet\tThe Minstrel Trainer is in Archet, west of the training grounds. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7554]="70018F53\n1\tUse the skill Deft Strike on a training-dummy\tSpeak with the trainer again and learn the skill Deft Strike. Use your new skill on the training-dummy nearby. NOTE: Use the trainer and select Train Warden Skills to open the skill selection panel. Left-click on a skill to highlight it and then left-click the Train button at the bottom of the skill selection panel, or double-click the skill, and you will successfully purchase the skill. HINT: Wardens use combinations of their basic skills such as Quick Thrust and Shield-Bash to build more powerful Gambit attacks. To use your Deft Strike skill, attack a Training-Dummy with your Quick Thrust ability twice. This should cause your Gambit Default skill to change into your Deft Strike skill. Use your Deft Strike ability to strike a Training-Dummy.\n2\tTalk to the Warden Trainer in Edhelion\tNow that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n3\tTalk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion\tDorongúr Whitethorn is in Edhelion. You should make your way to Dorongúr Whitethorn and tell him that you have finished your meditation and have prepared yourself for battle.\n",
[7555]="70062E61\n1\tTalk to Malavin\tWar-tyrant Akúlhun directed you to the war tent to speak with an Angmarim sorceress there named Malavin. Apparently she is here to assist, inspect, or guide the war effort. Whatever her purpose, it does not sit well with the War-tyrant.\n2\tSpeak with the emissaries\tMalavin instructed you to speak to each of the emissaries representing the clans of Carn Dûm and beyond. They have blessings that they will seek to bestow upon you, provided you will serve in their name.\n3\tTalk to Malavin\tHaving spoken to all the emissaries it is time to return to Malavin for further instruction.\n",
[7556]="700000CE\n1\tTalk to Amdir\tAmdir may be found resting on the ground near the centre of Archet, outside The Mad Badger Inn. The Ranger Amdir has spread word that he wishes to speak with you.\n",
[7557]="700248C0\n1\tTalk to Dwalin and tell him of Gormr's plans for the ritual\tDwalin is in Frerin's Court, in the very centre of the Thorin's Gate area. Now would be a good time to consult Dwalin on Gormr's strange behaviour and sinister hints.\n",
[7558]="70018F86\n1\tDefeat slugs in Edhelion (total: 4)\tSlugs infest a pool within the walls of Edhelion, east of Dorollas. Dorollas has tasked you with cleaning the slugs from Edhelion so that healing may begin in the once-beautiful refuge of the Elves.\n2\tTalk to Dorollas in Edhelion\tDorollas is west of the pool in Edhelion, near Elladan. You should return to Dorollas and tell him that you have successfully purged the vile slugs from the pool.\n",
[7559]="7000015C\n1\tTalk to Captain Brackenbrook\tCaptain Brackenbrook commands the garrison from The Mad Badger Inn to the south of Amdir. Amdir fears that Captain Brackenbrook will not heed his tidings of the traitor Calder Cob, but hopes that if the news comes from you, he will listen.\n2\tTalk to Amdir\tAmdir rests against the building north of The Mad Badger Inn. Captain Brackenbrook was not willing to hear what you had to say about Calder Cob. Instead, he told you to tell Amdir to stay out of Archet's troubles, after suggesting you help the local farms fend off wolves.\n",
[7560]="7002282D\n1\tTalk to Captain Brackenbrook in Archet\tCaptain Brackenbrook is in the town of Archet, near The Mad Badger Inn. You should speak with Captain Brackenbrook on Strider's behalf and try to convince him to heed the Blackwold threat.\n2\tSee if Kate Henseed will believe your warning\030See if Peg Pruner will believe your warning\030See if Constable Thistlewool will believe your warning\tThe townsfolk of Archet are standing around the town, the presence of Ranger guests having drawn their attention. You should speak to the townsfolk to see if anyone else is on your side and not Brackenbrook's.\n3\tTell Strider that the people of Archet do not believe you\tStrider is in the town of Archet, awaiting word. You should speak with Strider and tell him of Captain Brackenbrook's folly.\n",
[7561]="700194A4\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Surprise Strike\tEnter Use your Surprise Strike skill against the nearby training dummy. HINT: Burglars benefit greatly from Critical Strikes and Devastating Blows. Scoring such hits will allow them to use special skills such as Double-edged Strike. In addition, many Burglar skills benefit from being in Stealth. Try attacking a training-dummy from Stealth with Surprise Strike to inflict even more damage.\n2\tTalk to the Burglar Trainer in Archet\tThe Burglar Trainer is in Archet, west of the training grounds. Now that you have successfully used your Surprise Strike, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7562]="700248C1\n1\tDefeat barghests in the snow-fields around Frerin's Court (total: 4)\tBarghests can be found in the sooty snow-fields around Frerin's Court. You should defeat barghests, for they are a sign of an unnatural death in this valley that was once hale and fair.\n2\tTalk to Unnarr in Frerin's Court\tUnnarr is in Frerin's Court, standing among the other members of Dwalin's party. You should speak with Unnarr and tell him of your success in driving off the evil barrow-hounds in Thorin's Gate.\n",
[7563]="700244AF\n1\tSeek Merethen's insight on the riddle of Elrond's dream\tThe Elves of Elrond's Company can be found around the Edhelion Watch. You should seek out Elves with ideas on where to start investigating the dream.\n2\tSeek Dorollas' insight on the riddle of Elrond's dream\tThe Elves of Elrond's Company can be found around the Edhelion Watch. You should seek out Elves with ideas on where to start investigating the dream.\n3\tTalk to Elladan\tElladan waits on the road to Edhelion. You should speak with Elladan of what you learned from Merethen and Dorollas.\n",
[7564]="70024187\n1\tTalk to Elladan son of Elrond\tElladan, a son of Elrond Halfelven, stands not far from Nos Grimsong. You should speak with Elladan to learn on what errand the Elves of Rivendell have ventured so far into Ered Luin.\n",
[7565]="70001056\n1\tTalk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion\tDorongúr Whitethorn is at the bottom of the steps within the ruins of Edhelion, beyond the gate. Dorongúr Whitethorn wishes to speak to you about a matter of great importance.\n",
[7566]="70000E29\n1\tBring the dwarf-made sword to Dwalin\030Search a goblin prowler\tGoblin-prowlers are found to the south-west of Frerin's Court, lurking in the hills of the region. Dwalin has asked you to slay a goblin and search it. If you find anything interesting, return it to Dwalin at once.\n",
[7567]="700000D2\n1\tTalk to Elrohir\tElrohir may be found somewhere in the Mirkstone Tunnels. The entrance to the Tunnels lies at the bottom of the Axe-head Path, north-west of Frerin's Court. Elrohir, son of Elrond, entered the Mirkstone Tunnels to search for answers to the mystery of why the Dourhands have allied themselves with goblins. Dwalin asked you to meet with Elrohir to see what he may have learned.\n2\tBring the letter to Dwalin\tDwalin can be found in Frerin's Court, south-east of the Mirkstone Tunnels. Elrohir gave you a letter to take to Dwalin.\n",
[7568]="7000012B\n1\tTalk to Dwalin\tDwalin can be found in Frerin's Court, the central square of Thorin's Gate. Olin revealed that Gormr Dourhand is in league with goblins and may have contributed to his poisoning.\n",
[7569]="7002481C\n1\tTalk to Gormr Doursmith, Steward of Thorin's Hall\tGormr guards the door to the tomb at the Berghold, in the south of the Thorin's Gate area. You should speak with Gormr and find out what you can about his initiatives as Steward of Thorin's Hall and why Skorgrím's body has been moved.\n",
[7570]="7000012C\n1\tTalk to Olin\tOlin may be found to the west of Frerin's Court. Bolli asked you to find Olin, one of the Guards of the Silver Deep, and learn what he knows about the situation at Thorin's Hall.\n",
[7571]="70000EBE\n1\tStrider suggested you train further before coming to Archet's defence.\t\n2\tTalk to Strider in Archet\tStrider can be found outside The Mad Badger Inn in the centre of Archet. Now that you have spoken to the more experienced your class, you should return to Strider.\n",
[7572]="700244B0\n1\tClass trainers can be found in major hubs throughout the world, but the nearest is in the Edhelion Watch, not far from Elladan. You should speak with your trainer to see if they have anything for you to learn.\t\n2\tTalk to Elladan\tElladan waits on the road to Edhelion. You should speak with Elladan and let him know that you are prepared to face whatever dangers lie in your path.\n",
[7573]="70021D48\n1\tSpeak with Ned Pruner\tNed Pruner is in the jails to the east of Captain Brackenbrook's location.\n",
[7574]="70022A8E\n1\tDefeat brigands to thin their ranks (total: 4)\030Gather information about the intended Blackwold raid\tThe Blackwold's Roost can be found south of the Hunting Lodge. You should defeat brigands to thin their ranks and gather information about their exact plans for the raid on Archet.\n2\tBring the Blackwold-plans to Jon Brackenbrook\tJon Brackenbrook is mustering his strength in the Hunter's Lodge, in the north-east corner of Archet. You should return to Jon Brackenbrook with the Blackwold-plans you have collected.\n",
[7575]="70067347\n1\tUse your Thrust skill on the Training Dummy (total: 3)\tUse your skill Thrust on the training dummy nearby.\n2\tTalk to Barton Halifax, the Mariner Trainer in Archet\tBarton Halifax, the Mariner Trainer, is in Archet, west of the training grounds. Now that you have successfully used your skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[7576]="700248D7\n1\tCollect healing herbs from the Mirkstone Tunnels (total: 5)\tIt is possible that healing herbs may be found inside the cave behind Elrohir. You should search the cave for herbs that grow to help to purge the poisons from the Mirkstone Tunnels.\n2\tExamine the cave for what might be causing the blight of Ered Luin\tThere is surely a reason for the Dead to have encroached upon these parts, and this cave seems to be the source. You should search the cave for the heart of the problems at Thorin's Gate.\n3\tBring the healing herbs to Elrohir\tElrohir is outside the Mirkstone Tunnels, guarding the entrance from the bloodthirsty Dourhands. You should bring the herbs to Elrohir and tell him what you witnessed inside the caves.\n",
[7577]="7000104E\n1\tThe Elf your class is in the ruins near Dorongúr Whitethorn. Dorongúr suggested you speak to one of the Elves reflecting upon the events that happened in Edhelion so long ago. You must learn all you can from those who contemplate the past. Listen to their words and learn from their wisdom.\t\n",
[7578]="70018F55\n1\tDefeat insects near the trees of Edhelion (total: 4)\tThe insects may be found at the copse of trees north of Dorongúr Whitethorn, near the golden gate. Dorongúr Whitethorn charged you with helping to reclaim the refuge of Edhelion by eliminating the insects that have made the nearby trees their home.\n2\tTalk to Dorongúr Whitethorn in Edhelion\tDorongúr Whitethorn is south of the trees. With the insects defeated, you have proven yourself worthy to Dorongúr Whitethorn. You should return to him and tell him of your victory.\n",
[7579]="7000002C\n1\tCollect piles of bilberries (total: 4)\tBilberry bushes grow near Blackwold's Roost, south-east of Archet. Ned Pruner has asked you to gather enough bilberries to bake the cakes that Calder Cob demanded.\n2\tBring the berries to Ned Pruner\tNed Pruner can be found at Archet's jail. You collected the bilberries which Ned Pruner requested. You should return to Ned with the berries.\n",
[7580]="70007956\n1\tGather kingsfoil leaves (total: 4)\tKingsfoil grows south of Archet, near some old ruins called Bronwe's Folly. Celandine Brandybuck, too frightened to pass beyond the gates of Archet, has asked you to collect kingsfoil leaves for her, so that she can prepare the remedy Amdir asked her to make.\n2\tTalk to Celandine Brandybuck\030Collect Kingsfoil-leaf (total: 4)\tCelandine Brandybuck can be found with Amdir outside The Mad Badger Inn in Archet. You have gathered enough leaves for Amdir's remedy. You should return with them to Celandine Brandybuck.\n",
[7581]="700228A6\n1\tAsk Captain Brackenbrook for directions and begin to try to earn his favour\tCaptain Brackenbrook is near The Mad Badger Inn in the village of Archet. You should ask the Captain if he knows of any kingsfoil plants nearby and also if he would like some assistance to earn his favour.\n2\tComplete a quest for Calder Cob, Brackenbrook's most trusted soldier\030Gather kingsfoil leaves to treat Amdir's wound (total: 4)\tCalder Cob is at a farm outside of Archet, on the way to Bronwe's Folly as you take the road south from the town. Kingsfoil can be found at Bronwe's Folly. You should speak with Calder Cob and see how you can assist him against the threat of attacking wolves before heading to the ruins to pick kingsfoil.\n3\tReturn to Strider with the kingsfoil and your strange tale\tStrider is in the town of Archet, awaiting your return with leaves and news of your efforts to get Brackenbrook to trust you. You should bring Strider the kingsfoil and inform him of Calder Cob's treacherous behaviour.\n",
[7582]="70001081\n1\tTalk to Nos Grimsong in Frerin's Court\tNos Grimsong can be found in the north-west corner of Frerin's Court. Bolli instructed you to lend your aid to Nos Grimsong.\n",
[7583]="70000EBF\n1\tTalk to Dirk Mudbrick\tDirk Mudbrick defends a farm south and west out the front gate of Archet. Amdir told you to speak with Dirk Mudbrick and offer him your services, as Captain Brackenbrook originally instructed you.\n2\tDefeat wolves near Archet (total: 6)\tWolves can be found east and south of the farm and at Bronwe's Folly. Dirk Mudbrick is charged with guarding the sheep-farm outside of Archet and is pleased to be receiving help from Captain Brackenbrook.\n3\tTalk to Dirk Mudbrick\tDirk Mudbrick can be found at the sheep-farm south and west from Archet. You should return to Dirk Mudbrick with news of your success.\n",
[7584]="7000107F\n1\tThe your class trainer awaits you near the centre of Frerin's Court. Nos Grimsong suggested that you spend some time training with the visiting your class.\t\n2\tTalk to Bolli in Frerin's Court\tBolli can be found on the northern steps in the centre of Frerin's Court. You should return to Bolli and see what else he might have in store for you.\n",
})
